---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import InquiryForm from '../components/InquiryForm.astro';
---
<Layout title="Emergency Management & Consulting Services" description="Practical emergency planning, risk assessments, continuity planning, exercises, and improvement planning for Washington organizations.">
  <p class="lead">Useful plans begin with a clear understanding of your risks, your people, and the work you need to keep doing.</p>
  <p>I work with businesses, public agencies, healthcare organizations, nonprofits, and community organizations to strengthen preparedness. The starting point is your organization's needs—not a generic binder of plans.</p>
  <a class="button" href="#request">Request a Consultation</a>
  <div class="offering-grid">
    <section><h2>Emergency management programs</h2><p>Program development, preparedness assessments, policy development, and evaluation of responsibilities, resources, and coordination. Identify gaps and set practical priorities.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Emergency operations &amp; action plans</h2><p>Emergency operations plans, workplace emergency action plans, evacuation procedures, shelter-in-place planning, severe weather readiness, and emergency communications. Define who does what and how decisions are made.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Hazard &amp; vulnerability assessments</h2><p>Identify threats, vulnerabilities, and potential consequences. Use the assessment to guide preparedness work and focus limited resources where they will make a difference.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Continuity of operations &amp; business continuity</h2><p>Identify essential functions, dependencies, staffing needs, alternate ways of working, and recovery priorities so disruption does not leave your organization without a plan.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Organizational &amp; community preparedness</h2><p>Build preparedness programs that connect leadership, employees, partners, and the people you serve. Workshops can also cover workplace readiness, disaster preparedness, and family emergency planning.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Exercises, reviews &amp; improvement planning</h2><p>Tabletop exercises, emergency response drills, scenario-based training, and incident command familiarization. After-action reviews and improvement plans turn lessons into specific actions, owners, and follow-through.</p></section>
  </div>
  <h2>Start with the problem you need to solve</h2><p>Tell me what you are planning for, what already exists, and where you need assistance. We can discuss a realistic scope and timeframe before making any commitment.</p>
  <InquiryForm type="consulting" />
  <p class="service-disclaimer">I provide these services independently. My public office, employment, and volunteer affiliations do not constitute endorsement of this work.</p>
  <p>Looking for CPR or First Aid certification? <a href="/training/">Go directly to Training &amp; Certification.</a></p>
</Layout>
